# Inkling 2 Mini (stock), Basalt NVFP4-MX8: the RTX 5090 default since
# 2026-11-24 (Max; docs/reports/DECISIONS-2026-11-24.md §10).
#
# Exactly the serve of the measured row INK-T2-STOCK (campaign arm I_T2_stock,
# 53/71 scored, SCORE 78.2, single seed): Basalt v0.5.7 (400b411c), the stock
# pack jesdga/Inkling-2-Mini-Basalt @ c2afac3adb772e14d77b2ea2ac7068ad4460e932,
# file Inkling-2-Mini-NVFP4-MX8.basalt, sha256 28ec7072…1b99, 19,606,374,189
# bytes (evals/boards/v5/weights.json inkling2-mini-basalt-nvfp4-mx8-stock;
# pinned in scripts/weights.registry), served as
#   basalt serve --alias inkling-2-mini --parallel 1 --max-context 262144 --kv fp8
# with DSpark at the pack's default draft length (no flag) and the answer room
# at Basalt's default (auto: min(max(512, cap//4), cap//2) output tokens kept
# for the answer, so 6,144 thinking tokens of an 8,192-token turn). Those are
# the args `docker inspect` read at the arm's start and end
# (weights.json evidence). The serve record: the V5 Inkling report §10.1.
#
# ANSWER_ROOM and the PR #632 patch: the default arm ran unpatched with auto.
# PR #632 (upstream, open) changes what happens at the budget close (an
# answer block opens instead of the model being left to), not the reserve,
# so auto stays until the patched arm's decision says otherwise; change it
# here, with the arm that measured it, never in the adapter.
#
# Parsed by scripts/engines/basalt.sh (KEY=VALUE, never sourced).
PACK=Inkling-2-Mini-NVFP4-MX8.basalt
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=inkling-2-mini
PARALLEL=1
MAX_CONTEXT=262144
KV=fp8
ANSWER_ROOM=auto
# The agent setup measured with it (scripts/lib/conf.sh _ob_profile_set).
AGENT_PROFILE=inkling-best
# The board row this serve reproduces (evals/boards/v5/board.json).
MEASURED_ROW=INK-T2-STOCK
